Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||01-31-2001||06:57 PM||||Anyone ever replace the pump in the fuel tank with a remote electric line pump.<BR>I can see several places that one would fit but as the stock pump is only $30 I can just replace what I have.<BR>It would be nice not pulling the fuel tank next time I need to check the pump.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-01-2001||08:14 AM||||replace or add on? an 87 Iroc pump suited me just fine. if your stuck on adding a pump keep in mind the pumps don't like to siphon. if your going to add fittings to try and make it siphon out of the tank you'll just wipe out the pump. Jackson Racing tried this with their Civic supercharger kits and have since stoped and are including a better real fuel pump. the stock fuel pump can be shot with a kenne bell boost-a-pump that will help quite a bit. and you won't have to drop the tank.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||02-01-2001||08:34 AM||||If you do a search on a member named SPYDER<BR>he has a reply in there in which he says that for his V8 conversion he used an external fuel pump. He doesn't go into a lot of detail but you could email him.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||02-01-2001||05:00 PM||||Thanks for the tips, I found a cooked wire going to the fuel pump and need to replace it, a stock pump is $30 and probably the way I will go.<BR>I just dont want to do it twice.||||reg||1
